Photoshop 26.10.0's own layered RGB TIFFs saved with byte order IBM PC
(little-endian, "II") at 8 and 16 bits, from two takes of the private harness's
scripts/photoshop-probe/tiff_le_53_take.py (and its tiff_le_53.jsx; receipts in
~/devel/doctored-fixtures/photoshop/tiff-little-endian-53/take1 and take2).
Synthetic content the runner declared; Photoshop built and saved it.

Each take builds one document per depth from the runner's RGBA PNGs (no mode or
colour conversion): Bottom (full canvas, opaque); Top (opaque at x < top_keep,
transparent beyond) in the scene's blend mode and opacity; a group (Pass
Through) holding Inner (transparent outside inner_rect, opaque on its first
inner_opaque_rows rows and partial alpha below); Masked (full canvas, a Reveal
Selection user mask from mask_rect, then hidden). Every sample is the formula of
photoshop.json's "scenes" (core/tests/tiff_layers_little.rs restates it).
take1 is scene s1 (24 x 16, Multiply 60 %); take2 is the held-out scene s2
(19 x 13, odd row lengths, Screen 45 %, the non-ASCII name "Innér"), authored
after the reader was built from take1.

Each document was saved four times as a copy, in this order: layer compression
RLE then ZIP, each with byte order IBM then MACOS; layers and transparency on,
image compression NONE, profile embedded. The IBM files are here
(<scene>_<bits>_<rle|zip>_ibm.tif); of the MACOS twins only s2_8_rle_mac.tif and
s2_16_zip_mac.tif are (scripts/verify_mode_save_losses.py opens each beside its IBM
file), the rest stay in the receipts.
Against its twin, every IBM file's tag-37724 entries and records are the same
fields in the file's byte order, every four-character code byte-reversed (MIB8,
ryaL, 61rL), and every channel plane decodes to the twin's: the 8-bit RLE row
byte counts are little-endian, while the 16-bit Raw samples and ZIP-with-
prediction deltas are big-endian, as in the twin. Photoshop wrote Raw for every
16-bit channel under RLE layer compression.

photoshop.json holds both takes' run ids and the Photoshop version, the two
scenes' declarations, and per IBM file its sha256 and size, its twin's name and
sha256, Photoshop's rows of the file reopened, and the twin's records
(rectangle as top, left, bottom, right; blend key; opacity byte; flags; the
lsct section type; the mask) with each channel's compression word, rectangle
and the SHA-256 of its decoded plane, samples big-endian at the file's depth.
core/tests/tiff_layers_little.rs opens every file layered and checks it against
the formula (8 bits exact, 16 bits within 2 codes) and the twin's records and
plane hashes.
